Now let me write the domain module. First, double-check: is `src/domain/work/comment-range.test.ts` the style for tests? yes.

Design final:

`src/domain/work/comment-body.ts`:

```ts
/**
 * comment-body.ts — which characters of ONE comment a read returns, and the line
 * that says how to read the next part.
 *
 * `get_issue_comments` capped each comment at a fifth of the tool budget and said
 * how much it had dropped. That is not enough to be useful: the marker named a
 * count but no way to ask for the rest, so a comment whose decision was in its
 * last paragraph was unreadable through the tool — the only way back was to leave
 * it and fetch the comment's REST URL. Measured on #149: reads came back cut at
 * 1,600 characters, again and again, with the tail the reader wanted never
 * arriving.
 *
 * `files/read` already had the answer: take an offset, and name the offset to
 * continue from in the text. This is the same shape for a comment body, where
 * there is no line numbering to count and the unit is an offset in characters.
 */

export interface CommentBody {
  /** The segment, with any marker saying what was left out and how to continue. */
  text: string;
  /** The `body_offset` that reads the next segment; absent when this one reaches the end. */
  next?: number;
}

export function readCommentBody(
  body: string,
  { index, budget, offset = 0 }: { index: number; budget: number; offset?: number },
): CommentBody {
  ...
}
```

Wait — should the marker say `from: N`? The index is the comment's number within the issue, which equals the `from` value. Yes.

Let me write precise implementation:

```ts
export function readCommentBody(body, {index, budget, offset = 0}) {
  const start = offset;
  const remaining = body.length - start;
  const ended = () => ...;
  const prefix = start === 0 ? "" : `\n[continuing comment ${index} at character ${start + 1} of ${body.length}]\n`;
  const restFits = remaining + prefix.length <= budget;
  if (restFits) {
    return { text: prefix.length ? `${prefix}${body.slice(start)}` : body.slice(start) };
  }
  const marker = (shown: number) =>
    `\n\n[${start + shown} of ${body.length} characters shown; ${remaining - shown} dropped from the end. ` +
    `Read the rest of comment ${index} with from: ${index}, body_offset: ${start + shown}]`;
  const reserve = Math.max(marker(0).length, marker(remaining).length);
  const shown = Math.min(remaining, Math.max(1, budget - prefix.length - reserve));
  return { text: prefix + body.slice(start, start + shown) + marker(shown), next: start + shown };
}
```

Check the length bound: text length = prefix + shown + marker(shown). marker(shown).length ≤ reserve (by construction? marker(0) has max digits in "dropped" and "start+0"; marker(remaining) has max digits in "shown"/"start+remaining" and dropped=0. Is marker(shown) always ≤ max of those two? The digit counts: `start+shown` digits grows with shown → max at remaining. `remaining-shown` digits max at 0. Sum of digit counts ≤ max(a,b) since digits(x)+digits(y) ≤ digits(x+y)+1 ≤ max digits + 1... hmm. Let R = remaining, s=shown, S=start. Numbers: A = S+s (digits ≤ digits(S+R) = digits(body.length)), B = R-s (digits ≤ digits(R)). marker length depends on digits(A)+digits(B) plus prefix `[${...} of ${body.length}]`. digits(A)+digits(B): A+B = S+R, so digits(A)+digits(B) ≤ digits(S+R)+1 = digits(body.length)+1. marker(0) gives A=S (digits(S)) + B=R (digits(R)) ≤ digits(S+R)+1 too. And marker(remaining) gives digits(S+R)+digits(0)=digits(body.length)+1. So max(marker(0), marker(remaining)) has at least digits(S+R)+1 digits. Good enough: reserve is ≥ marker(shown) always. 

Edge: if `budget - prefix - reserve <= 0` we set shown = 1 and text length may exceed budget slightly. Guarded by comment. Fine, or clamp: `const room = Math.max(1, ...)`.

Hmm, what about the case where the body is cut but `remaining <= budget` while prefix makes it exceed? Then restFits false and we cut even though only the prefix pushes over — shown = min(remaining, room) so we'd cut a little and emit a marker naming offset. That's correct enough.

Also: should the *first* segment when offset=0 and body fits return `text: body` unchanged? Yes.

Markers and JSON: fine.

Now one subtlety: `offset` = body.length exactly. Then remaining 0, restFits true → returns prefix + "" = "[continuing comment 3 at character 4001 of 4000]", weird. Tool will validate offset < length (unless length 0). For empty body with offset 0, remaining 0 → returns "". Fine.

Tool-side validation:

```ts
const offset = a.body_offset ?? 0;
if (a.body_offset !== undefined) {
  if (range.count !== 1) {
    mcpFail(
      "`body_offset` reads past a cut in ONE comment, so it needs a range naming exactly one: " +
      `this read selects ${range.count ? `comment(s) ${range.from}-${range.to} of ${all.length}` : `nothing (${range.showing})`}. ` +
      "Pass `from` naming the comment whose marker gave the offset."
    );
