// reason the tail of #149's comments never arrived. One comment now gets 8,000.
const perCommentBudget = Math.floor(TOOL_OUTPUT_BUDGET / Math.max(1, range.count));
```

Wait: should I floor at something? For 20 comments, 400 each. The `read`-style continuation handles the rest. OK.

Hmm, but does this make behavior worse for, e.g., default window 5 comments (1600 each, same as before) — yes same.

Now selected map:

```ts
const offset = a.body_offset ?? 0;
const selected = (range.count > 0 ? all.slice(range.from - 1, range.to) : []).map((comment) => {
  const body = (comment as { body?: unknown }).body;
